<protocol name="execution_flows" type="orchestration" agent="pm">

## PURPOSE

Execution patterns after user approval. ID tracking, junction rules, delegation templates.
Load when: User approved execution, ready to delegate to specialists.

---

## CATALOG ADDITION FLOWS

**User chooses what and in what order. PM routes accordingly:**

### Flow A: Catalog Only (no image)

```
User: "Just add to catalog" / "entry only"
PM -> catalog_specialist: Create product (no asset_id)
     <- Returns: product_id
[DONE] Product exists without image. User can add image later.
```

### Flow B: Image Only (with asset)

```
User: "Process the image" / "create the asset"
PM -> creative_specialist: Create asset
     <- Returns: asset_id
[DONE] Asset exists, not linked. User can create catalog entry later.
```

### Flow C: Image Only (ephemeral)

```
User: "Download only" / "just for me"
PM -> creative_specialist: "Standalone - no asset record"
     <- Returns: storage_path (no asset_id)
[DONE] File in pending/. No asset record. Cannot link to catalog.
```

### Flow D: Catalog First (2 steps)

```
User: "Catalog first, then images"

Step 1: PM -> catalog_specialist: Create product (no asset_id)
        <- Returns: product_id (CAPTURE THIS)

Step 2: PM -> creative_specialist: Create asset, product_id=[product_id]
        <- Creative creates asset + product_assets junction
        <- Returns: asset_id

[DONE] Product + Asset + Junction all exist.
```

**Key:** Creative handles junction when given product_id (same pattern as campaign_assets).

### Flow E: Images First (standard)

```
User: "Images first" / "yes" / "full flow"

Step 1: PM -> creative_specialist: Create asset
        <- Returns: asset_id

Step 2: PM -> catalog_specialist: Create product, asset_id=[asset_id]
        <- Returns: product_id + junction

[DONE] Product + Asset + Junction all exist.
```

---

## ID TRACKING

**PM captures from Step 1, passes to Step 2:**

| Flow | Step 1 Returns | Pass to Step 2 | Step 2 Creates |
|------|----------------|----------------|----------------|
| Catalog first | product_id | product_id -> creative | Asset + junction |
| Images first | asset_id | asset_id -> catalog | Product + junction |

**Both specialists can create product_assets junctions.** Whoever runs second receives the existing ID and creates the junction.

---

## CREATIVE->CATALOG ASSET HANDOFF

**Creative specialist creates asset records (with HITL), catalog specialist creates product + junction.**

### Why Creative Owns Assets

| Concern | Old Model (storage_path) | New Model (asset_id) |
|---------|-------------------------|----------------------|
| Image rejection feedback | Goes to catalog_specialist (wrong expert) | Goes to creative_specialist (right expert) |
| Iteration on visual issues | Back-and-forth PM<->creative | Creative iterates directly |
| HITL focus | Mixed: image + catalog in one | Separated: image quality, then catalog data |
| Expert handling | Catalog specialist can't fix images | Image expert handles image feedback |

### Flow

```
[1. creative_specialist] -> processes image
      |
      v
[creative_specialist calls write_data: CREATE asset] -> [HITL: "Is this image acceptable?"]
      |
      +---> REJECTED: Creative iterates, resubmits
      |
      +---> APPROVED: Asset created
      |
      v
[Returns asset_id to PM]
      |
      v
[2. PM receives asset_id]
      |
      v
[3. PM delegates to catalog_specialist]:
   "Create product entry with existing asset.
    Read analysis files for context.
    Asset already approved: [asset_id]
    Create product + product_assets junction."
      |
      v
[4. catalog_specialist] -> creates:
   - Product record (if new)
   - product_assets junction linking asset_id to product
   [HITL approval for catalog data]
```

### Two-Stage HITL (Intentional)

| Stage | Owner | HITL Question | User Focus |
|-------|-------|---------------|------------|
| 1. Asset creation | creative_specialist | "Is this image acceptable?" | Visual quality, accuracy |
| 2. Catalog entry | catalog_specialist | "Is this product data correct?" | SKU, pricing, family, attributes |

